review:
If you're as much of a cyberpunk fan as I am, [b]I highly recommend this game[/b] : it takes a lot of inspiration from the best works in the genre such as Cyberpunk 2020, Altered Carbon, Shadowrun, Neuromancer, etc. And if you're a fan of the genre you will enjoy the amazing artistic direction and world design and take great pleasure in recognizing the different things they took inspiration from in the cyberpunk genre.

Pros : 
[list]
  [*] One of the most well realized artistic directions and world designs in the genre, only rivaled by the likes of RUINER or Cyberpunk 2077 ;
  [*] Very good lore and worldbuilding ;
  [*] Very fun and intense combat ;
  [*] High build variety with loads of options to specialize your character ;
  [*] Killer soundtrack and fantastic sound design overall ;
  [*] Coop multiplayer, and a very good one as well.
[/list]

Cons : 
[list]
  [*] Lack of a sprint button or good mobility option to traverse the world ; 
  [*] Unengaging main story, the game fails at making you care about any of the events, you're just ordered around doing tasks left and right ;
  [*] Characters for the most part are boring and forgettable, no character development whatsoever ;
  [*] Extremely disappointing final boss and anti-climatic ending ;
  [*] Weird difficulty spikes at some points ;
  [*] A few game-breaking bugs here and there like getting stuck on some objects or clipping through the ground ;
  [*] Occasional performance issues.
[/list]
